--swiftversion 6.0
--indent 4
--maxwidth 150

# Match the existing codebase's house style rather than impose a new one:
# - compact single-line `if`/`for` bodies (`if x { return }`) are used pervasively as a terse
#   guard-clause convention — wrapIfStatementBodies/wrapLoopBodies would rewrite ~150 files.
# - trailing line comments are hand-aligned in columns with extra spaces
#   (`x = 1          // why`) — consecutiveSpaces would collapse that alignment.
# - `//` vs `///` is chosen deliberately per CLAUDE.md ("only comment the non-obvious WHY"),
#   not "every API gets a doc comment" — docComments would fight that.
# - compact multi-statement seed/test lines (`a = 1; b = 2`) — semicolons would split them.
--disable redundantSelf,semicolons,wrapMultilineStatementBraces,wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapLoopBodies,consecutiveSpaces,docComments,trailingCommas,andOperator,sortImports

--exclude build,DerivedData,.build
